{
  "id": "COMPOUND:21151 - PROTEIN:4972",
  "verbalization": "Schisanhenol B is implicated in the biological activity of LAMA-84 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Schisanhenol B acts as a target for multiple entities, with MIP, 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One, and S-ethylcysteine zwitterion all being targets of Schisanhenol B. These targets are ultimately linked to LAMA-84, indicating a potential pathway where Schisanhenol B influences the activity of these molecules, which in turn affect LAMA-84. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism where Schisanhenol B modulates the activity of other compounds, which may then interact with LAMA-84. The evidence supports a role for Schisanhenol B in the regulation of LAMA-84 through a series of molecular targets, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
